      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "heading",
            "level": 3,
            "text": "i. Combustion of alcohols"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "Alcohols when ignited, undergo complete combustion to form carbon dioxide and water."
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3-CH2-OH + 3O2 -> 2CO2 + 3H2O} \\qquad \\Delta H^\\circ_c = -1367\\ \\text{kJ mol}^{-1}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃–CH₂–OH + 3O₂ → 2CO₂ + 3H₂O    ΔH°c = −1367 kJ mol⁻¹"
          },
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "The above reaction is highly exothermic; this is why the alcohol is used as an alternate to petrol in some countries."
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
